#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# conjugacy_class_representatives

#% text
# `conjugacy_class_representatives(G)`: one element of each conjugacy class

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Classes are ordered by the order of their elements, then by size; the identity comes first.

#% item
# Groups of at most 2000000 elements are enumerated; larger ones get representatives from random elements, tested for conjugacy, until the class sizes add up to the group order.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
conjugacy_class_representatives(symmetric_group(4))
#% output
#= [cycles([]), cycles([[1, 3], [2, 4]]), cycles([[1, 2]]), cycles([[1, 3, 4]]), cycles([[1, 4, 2, 3]])]

#% cell
length(conjugacy_class_representatives(mathieu_group(12)))
#% output
#= 15

